  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $G$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. For any $f(x)\\in G,$ we have $1\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\nII. For any $f(x)\\in G$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha -\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)-\\beta f(x).$\n\nIII. The scalar multiplication of functions in $G$ is associative.",
